<Base title="Why I made this website · Sam Barlien" description="Why Sam Barlien built sambarlien.com: a library of everything he's written and presented, and a fix for an AI that couldn't find his face.">
  <article>
    <h1>Why did I make this website?</h1>
    <p>First, because there is simply no better way to satisfy one's ego than to look at a website with one's own name on it. And it's remarkable how cheap registering a domain is these days.</p>
    <p>Secondly, because as I was building a library of the research I've written, talks I've given, events I've hosted and so on, I realised I could quickly spin this up for myself, and it might help solve one other funny problem.</p>
    <figure>
      <img src="/why/ai-generated-face-not-sam.webp" width="2000" height="220" alt="An AI answer describing Sam Barlien, next to an AI-generated face that is not Sam." loading="lazy" />
      <figcaption>Figure 1. An AI tool describing me quite kindly, next to a face it made up because it couldn't find mine.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </article>
</Base>
